flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the lens<br/>front element at oblique incidence for scratches or<br/>chips. 2. Check the lens housing for impact cracks<br/>or loose retaining ring. 3. Inspect the lens mount<br/>face for contamination or swarf."]
    box_2{"Lens scratches, chips or contamination present?"}
    box_3(["End, Replace lens: optical damage detected"])
    box_4["Position the lux meter probe at the focal plane of<br/>the imaging lens, centred on the inspection zone,<br/>with no part present. Record illuminance in lux and<br/>compare against the minimum level in the lighting<br/>specification. Repeat at the four corners of the<br/>inspection field to check uniformity and note any<br/>zone where illuminance drops below 80% of the centre<br/>value."]
    box_5[/"Refer to the vision system lighting specification."/]
    box_6{"Lighting intensity within specified range at part<br/>plane?"}
    box_7["Adjust lighting voltage or replace LEDs as required"]
    box_8["Blow dry compressed air across the lens surface to<br/>remove loose particles. Apply two drops of optical<br/>lens cleaner to a lint free cloth and wipe the lens<br/>surface using a single outward spiral motion from<br/>centre to edge. Inspect the lens under oblique light<br/>after cleaning and repeat if smearing or residue is<br/>visible."]
    box_9["Display the live image and position a high contrast<br/>resolution target at the nominal focal distance.<br/>Using the image analysis software, measure the<br/>modulation transfer function at line pairs per<br/>millimetre specified in the lens acceptance<br/>criteria. Record the sharpness value and note which<br/>quadrant of the field, if any, shows the greatest<br/>drop in contrast."]
    box_10[/"Refer to the focus target specification."/]
    box_11{"Image sharpness within sharpness specification<br/>specification?"}
    box_12["Adjust focus ring or working distance to<br/>specification"]
    box_13{"Reverify focus after lens adjustment"}
    box_14(["End, Escalate: focus unrecoverable, lens or mount<br/>fault"])
    box_15["Install the grid distortion target at the nominal<br/>focal distance with the grid centred on the optical<br/>axis. Capture a still image and use the vision<br/>software distortion analysis tool to measure radial<br/>distortion at the four corner grid intersections and<br/>at the field centre. Compare the maximum distortion<br/>value against the tolerance in the camera<br/>calibration specification."]
    box_16{"Distortion within ±0.5 px at corner positions?"}
    box_17["Apply lens distortion correction coefficients in<br/>vision software"]
    box_18["Place the standard chessboard calibration target on<br/>the presentation fixture at the nominal focal<br/>distance. Capture five images from five different<br/>target orientations as required by the calibration<br/>algorithm. Run the calibration routine in the vision<br/>software and record the reprojection error; confirm<br/>the result is below the limit stated in the vision<br/>system commissioning record."]
    box_19[/"Refer to the vision calibration procedure."/]
    box_20{"Calibration residual error within 0.1 px root mean<br/>square?"}
    box_21["Rerun calibration with new target images, 20 poses<br/>minimum"]
    box_22{"Reverify calibration residual after recalibration"}
    box_23(["End, Escalate: calibration residual persistent,<br/>contact vision engineer"])
    box_24["Connect an oscilloscope channel to the part arrival<br/>sensor output and a second channel to the camera<br/>trigger signal. With the conveyor running, measure<br/>the delay between sensor rising edge and camera<br/>trigger rising edge. Compare the measured delay<br/>against the target timing in the system parameter<br/>record, adjusting the trigger delay register in the<br/>vision controller until within tolerance."]
    box_25{"Trigger delay within ±0.5 ms of specification?"}
    box_26["Adjust trigger delay in programmable controller<br/>programme"]
    box_27["Run 200 known good conforming parts through the<br/>inspection system in normal production conditions.<br/>Record the number flagged as reject by the system.<br/>Calculate the false reject rate as a percentage of<br/>the 200 part sample and compare against the maximum<br/>allowed false reject rate specified for the product.<br/>Document the part types and the inspection feature<br/>most frequently causing false rejections."]
    box_28{"False reject rate below 0.5%?"}
    box_29["Complete the following checks: 1. Retrieve the<br/>stored rejection images for the last ten false<br/>accepts. 2. Confirm each retrieved image shows a<br/>visible defect. 3. Compare the defect position<br/>against the inspection zone boundary settings."]
    box_30["Pass 10 known non conforming parts, each with a<br/>documented defect type, through the inspection<br/>system individually. Record whether each defect is<br/>detected and the system output for each part.<br/>Confirm that the system correctly rejects all 10<br/>parts; any part that is accepted constitutes a false<br/>accept and requires immediate investigation before<br/>resuming production."]
    box_31{"All known rejects correctly detected?"}
    box_32(["End, Escalate: detection capability insufficient,<br/>algorithm review required"])
    box_33["Export calibration data and update vision system log"]
    box_34["Log all test results and update maintenance record"]
    box_35(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_36["Secondary lens adjustment: clean all optical<br/>surfaces with dry nitrogen and reseat the lens body<br/>firmly in the mount before tightening the retaining<br/>ring. Check the lens mount datum face for swarf or<br/>contamination that would cause tilt. Adjust the<br/>focus drive mechanism in 0.1 turn increments and<br/>allow the mount to settle before returning to the<br/>sharpness measurement step."]

